      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Забы́л соль: he forgot the salt.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3280
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Вчера́ у нас был крити́к. У нас: at our place, like у меня́; нас is мы.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||И его́ о́тзыв хоро́ший.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:u1xnn2'
    '|a||Я сде́лал оши́бку. Оши́бка. Но э́то не пробле́ма!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:24m1g2'
    '|b||Хотя́ суп был без со́ли, о́тзыв хоро́ший.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3600
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1bbif45'
    '|a||Хотя́ means although. It brings in the minus, and the rest happens anyway. This colour marks the turn words.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1nbpxjx'
    '|a||О́тзыв хоро́ший, хотя́ суп был без со́ли. It can come first or second, as in English.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:vwysbf'
    '|a||Посмотри́те. Суп был без со́ли, зато́ ры́ба была́ вку́сная.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:odzo0g'
    '|a||Зато́: after a minus, a plus that makes up for it. Но is just but; зато́ brings the good side.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:3tgukk'
    '|b||Несмотря́ на оши́бку, о́тзыв хоро́ший.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2520
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:16n6xti'
    '|a||Несмотря́ на means despite.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1jugubj'
    '|a||So what''s the difference? Хотя́ суп был без со́ли: after хотя́, a whole sentence, with its verb.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:vva25z'
    '|a||Несмотря́ на оши́бку: after несмотря́ на, just a noun, in the accusative. Оши́бка, оши́бку.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:12w4e2o'
    '|a||Несмотря́ на дождь: despite the rain. Дождь stays дождь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:u6g35a'
    '|a||Крити́к всё равно́ написа́л хоро́ший о́тзыв. The minus changed nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:b6ycl2'
    '|b||А вот о́тзыв. Так как ры́ба была́ о́чень вку́сная, я приду́ ещё раз.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:6vhgoj'
    '|a||Так как: since, like потому́ что, but more formal, and it can open the sentence.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:tcguvp'
    '|a||Ве́чером звони́т Ма́ша. Tap Practise after the dialogue, and be me.':
